{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10\\cdot 1-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(10x-{x}^{4}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}]-[10\\cdot 0-{0}^{4}] \\\\  & =10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\pi +25{\\pi }^{4}"] ["math" "10\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}"] ["math" "10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}"] ["math" "\\pi -5{\\pi }^{4}"] ["math" "\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-51122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-346553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-346553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =2(2-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{3}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. We can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-9(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "-6\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "12\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "9\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352644" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352644" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 100({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (100{sec}^{2}⁡x-100)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-100\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-100x+C"] ["math" "-100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100+C"] ["math" "-100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C"] ["math" "100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100+C"] ["math" "100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-362530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3(1)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x+7}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+7}-\\sqrt{1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =3-2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-362529" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362529" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-2\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the cosecant-cotangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-0-(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352697" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352697" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-{sec}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-114457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)({csc}^{2}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-362804" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-362804" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =(5x+\\pi ),$ we get \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )={sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (9[1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )]-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (9{sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi ))-5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})={cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})|\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352742" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352742" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =3x-2\\pi ,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7[1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi )])\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+7(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-10567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}+4({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1))]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+4x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}+4(1)]-[{0}^{3}+4(0)] \\\\  & =5-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf73387de54e9c7c63b6f73806859506847c73a7e7ed1b4ed572e4ad134d84c9"} {"question" "q-352747" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "q-352747" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/state.json" "file_sha256" "793e6f55c7291245448dfc78dbc7b7ec11ede3b9951e690f839f63c89e13f104"} {"question" "e-477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-477.json" "file_sha256" "33a6fb5067d0a9efaf01c1f5cedcb1ea3a49856e6344dcc1c050d26e6b496184"} {"question" "e-477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-477.json" "file_sha256" "33a6fb5067d0a9efaf01c1f5cedcb1ea3a49856e6344dcc1c050d26e6b496184"} {"question" "e-478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-478.json" "file_sha256" "5aa058c8db4b888fa28de731cf2c707eac712f54c3919fed45d4e65cb913a59a"} {"question" "e-478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-478.json" "file_sha256" "5aa058c8db4b888fa28de731cf2c707eac712f54c3919fed45d4e65cb913a59a"} {"question" "e-479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-479.json" "file_sha256" "39c8e5a4f8461de8bb14161ec0e580a0d969324edd6bf19157b6e231fc7ee934"} {"question" "e-479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-479.json" "file_sha256" "39c8e5a4f8461de8bb14161ec0e580a0d969324edd6bf19157b6e231fc7ee934"} {"question" "e-480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-480.json" "file_sha256" "6d7fc04f1faa3094ccb11ab419906960d3c2515446565e5b1d0a57f11ed2bf6f"} {"question" "e-480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-480.json" "file_sha256" "6d7fc04f1faa3094ccb11ab419906960d3c2515446565e5b1d0a57f11ed2bf6f"} {"question" "q-49326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "65d2dd5b1e3d49c4b44af352ffab1ec7696e2b3d08200aec4c1c4d80b7644ca2" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "The original question screenshot has bounds −π/6 to π/6. On this interval, 1−tan²x is nonzero, so the integrand simplifies to 9(1+tan²x)=9sec²x. Thus the integral is 9[tan x] from −π/6 to π/6 = 6√3, original option d (index 3). The authentic worked solution agrees and the saved submission was graded Correct. The database instead records upper bound π/3, explaining its 12√3 key; preserve the distinction rather than equating the answers." "bindings" {"problem" "b271455a3875d1e8053e91e2c01a64b37ed87657b19af56865b36138512d1ff4" "worked_solution" "6da3144b4cb70a74ca4e31c607ae0480579995ae49952bd7db07bb602a6ad442" "original_field" "20cb97d8c5d8964379665b09e9b8dc167ebb26a4e5332db0205ae45118c4d7e8" "reviewed_field" "c609b06209f36dc34e98582e41a7d7608c3404dc2e390b067ee283e096bd7209" "raw_widget" "96a6c5391e2afd24dc0c7bd198041d9777163b6950e75b8615cc0157722e66fb"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-49326-before.png" "sha256" "8a7ea61b74ea57bf04945dd04ffe13ddf4aa0d313ce0f1aaaea45f389e3a2a30"} {"path" "history-q-49326.png" "sha256" "26b3e497201e9516dfd6e4f91fe053ed077231b5048bf64163387e6901bcc3f5"} {"path" "q-49326-after.json" "sha256" "441fa46d8de4d8f3dade8e7a76b2a40844e6fcb3d431763d21f23def2c89858e"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "74eeb3039e91c3ba1c7edcaf7f008b28ba8a4284eb7367263d48e6dae1010929"}]} {"question" "q-49326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "-6\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "12\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "9\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "65d2dd5b1e3d49c4b44af352ffab1ec7696e2b3d08200aec4c1c4d80b7644ca2" "rationale" "The original question screenshot has bounds −π/6 to π/6. On this interval, 1−tan²x is nonzero, so the integrand simplifies to 9(1+tan²x)=9sec²x. Thus the integral is 9[tan x] from −π/6 to π/6 = 6√3, original option d (index 3). The authentic worked solution agrees and the saved submission was graded Correct. The database instead records upper bound π/3, explaining its 12√3 key; preserve the distinction rather than equating the answers."}] "usage" {"e-479" [] "q-10563" [] "e-480" [] "e-477" [] "e-478" [] "q-51122" [] "q-49326" [] "q-49447" []} "basis" 1126 "retractions" [[17592186097199 :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{π}(10\\cos^{2} x - 4x^{3} + 10\\sin^{2} x)dx$?"] [17592186097233 :question/problem "Calculate $∫\\frac{1}{1 - \\sin x}dx$."] [17592186097195 :question/problem "Evaluate $∫_{- π/6}^{π/3}\\frac{9 - 9\\tan^{4} x}{1 - \\tan^{2} x}dx$."] [17592186097195 :question/answer-fields 17592186095527] [17592186096855 :question/problem "Calculate $∫100\\tan^{2} xdx$."] [17592186096390 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096390 :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{1}{1 - \\sin^{2} x}dx &= ∫\\frac{1}{\\cos^{2} x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫(\\frac{1}{\\cos x})^{2}dx \\\\\n&= ∫\\sec^{2} xdx \\\\\n&= \\tan x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096391 :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096391 :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity\n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\tan x -x+C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096392 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096392 :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x\n$$\n\nRearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096393 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x$."] [17592186096393 :question/worked-solution "From the identity\n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\theta = 3x\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\ \\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right) \\\\ &= 2\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C \\\\ &= \\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093538 17592186093539 17592186093540 17592186093541 17592186093542 17592186095528 17592186095529 17592186095530 17592186095531 17592186095532 17592186095552 17592186095553 17592186095554 17592186095555 17592186095556 17592186095756 17592186095757 17592186095758 17592186095759 175921